          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಯಿರಿ (kāyiri) — \"please wait\", the polite form of ಕಾಯು (kāyu), \"to wait\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಒಂದು ನಿಮಿಷ ಕಾಯಿರಿ (ondu nimiṣa kāyiri) — \"please wait a minute\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಯಿರಿ (kāyiri) is native Dravidian: the polite command of kāyu, \"to guard, keep watch, wait\", which DEDR 1416 lists with Tamil kā, \"to guard\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The polite ending ‑ಇರಿ asks gently."
