            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೇಳಿಸಲಿಲ್ಲ (kēḷisalilla) — \"(it) was not heard\", the way to say \"I didn't hear\". It is built on ಕೇಳು, \"hear, listen\", with ‑ಇಲ್ಲ, \"not\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೇಳಿಸಲಿಲ್ಲ (kēḷisalilla) is native Dravidian: kēḷisu, \"to be heard\", from kēḷu, \"to hear\" (DEDR 2017), and illa, \"not\" (DEDR 2559). It is \"it was not heard\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A known verb with a known no."
